==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Machette_kos.pg.jpg|thumb|right|250px|a machete]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/məˈʃɛ.ti/|/məˈtʃɛ.ti/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-ncalif-machete.ogg|Audio (US, Northern California)|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|es|en}} {{m|es|machete}}, diminutive of {{m|es|macho||sledgehammer}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|mattea}}, cognate with Old French {{m|fro|machier}}, French {{m|fr|massue}}, English {{m|fr|mace}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sword]]-like [[tool]] used for [[cut]]ting large [[plant]]s with a [[chop]]ping motion. A machete's blade is usually 50 to 65 centimeters ([[cm]]) long, and up to three millimeters ([[mm]]) thick.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|bolo}}

